      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>We don't cite a figure we haven't read at its primary source, and we don't publish a statistic we can't attribute. Where real information doesn't yet exist for something this site could otherwise show — a metric, a case study, a named team member — we say so plainly rather than filling the gap with an invented number. If you find a citation on this site that's gone stale or broken, we'd want to know: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

